{{> Start this}}

{{> Logo this}}

{{> EmailTitle title=(t "This Address Already Has an Account") }}

{{!--
  Sent to the new address when someone asks to make it their account's and
  another account already uses it (#9821, Common's EmailChangeConfirmation).
  The page that asked says only that it is waiting for a confirmation, as it
  says for every address, so the person who typed it learns nothing from it;
  this email, to the address itself, is where it is said. Nothing changed,
  and there is no link to confirm.

  In the language, and with the time zone, of the account that has the
  address (#10157): its reader is that account's person, whoever asked. The
  product's name goes into a sentence through ttHtml, the request's rows
  are values, and everything else is OneUptime's own words in the reader's
  language (Utils/EmailLanguage.ts).
--}}

{{> InfoBlock info=(ttHtml "Someone asked to use this email address for another {{product}} account. This address already has an account, so it cannot be used for a second one, and nothing was changed." product=(brandName))}}

{{> InfoBlock info=(tHtml "If you asked for this, sign in with this address instead, or use a different address for the other account.")}}

{{> ButtonBlock buttonUrl=signInLink buttonText=(t "Sign In")}}

{{> VerticalSpace this}}

{{#if requestedAt}}
{{> InfoBlock info=(tHtml "Details of the request:")}}

{{> DetailBoxStart this }}
{{> DetailBoxField title=(t "Requested at:") plainText=requestedAt }}
{{> RequestOriginFields this }}
{{> DetailBoxEnd this }}
{{/if}}

{{> InfoBlock info=(tHtml "Didn't ask for this? You can safely ignore this email. Your account is unchanged, and whoever typed your address was not told that it has an account.")}}

{{> SupportBlock this }}

{{> Footer this}}

{{> End this}}
